/**
 * @page reference Reference guide
 *
 * This reference covers the daemon's own sources. Applications integrate through the wire
 * contract, not through any of these types: see @ref wire_contract and docs/protocol.md.
 *
 * The daemon combines llamad::Engine, llamad::ChatFormat and llamad::LlamaService, with
 * conversion between wire messages and engine types in llamad::wire and command-line reading
 * in llamad::cli.
 *
 * Only llamad-owned sources are indexed. Vendored llama.cpp, generated protobuf
 * sources and test fixtures are outside the API reference. The executable examples
 * are included in the source browser; tests are described on @ref testing.
 *
 * @see wire_contract
 * @see testing
 */

/**
 * @page wire_contract Wire contract
 *
 * The daemon exposes `llamad.v1.Llama` on a mode-0600 Unix domain socket. Requests
 * contain their entire history and tool definitions; the server keeps no sessions
 * and executes no tools. LlamaService translates requests to plain engine and chat
 * types through llamad::wire.
 *
 * A successful generation stream is zero or more `text` chunks and then exactly one
 * `finish` chunk carrying statistics and a finish reason. Transport errors or client
 * cancellation can end a stream before that chunk. Tool calls are atomic and appear only on
 * the `finish` chunk with TOOL_CALLS. Embed returns one L2-normalised vector per input and is
 * served only by an embedding model, which in turn serves no generation. Caller errors map to
 * INVALID_ARGUMENT, a missing capability (no usable chat template, or the wrong kind of model
 * for the RPC) to FAILED_PRECONDITION, and other failures to INTERNAL.
 *
 * Doxygen has no Protocol Buffers parser. The authoritative, commented schema is
 * included verbatim so message fields, numbers and defaults stay tied to the source.
 * @verbinclude proto/llamad/v1/llamad.proto
 */

/**
 * @page testing Tests and executable examples
 *
 * CTest runs model-free executable tests: chat_format_test.cpp checks real template
 * rendering and canned tool output; engine_test.cpp checks the prompt-cache bookkeeping;
 * flags_test.cpp checks the command-line reader and the shared engine flags; wire_test.cpp
 * checks conversion between wire messages and engine types, and checks each converted
 * message's descriptor so that a field added to llamad.proto fails until it is converted.
 *
 * tests/engine_smoke.cpp exercises raw generation, grammar constraints, cancellation,
 * chat rendering and embeddings in-process. It needs a local GGUF model and is not a CTest test.
 * tests/engine_bench.cpp measures prefill and decode tokens per second the same way; see
 * docs/performance.md.
 * docs/building.md describes the build, test and smoke-test scripts.
 */
